 on the subject is settled; its residual names the observation that would decide |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1139:the observation that would establish it. The end never decides a\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1164:## 4. Totality and refinement\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1179:indeterminate assessment report and an unperformed assessment take the\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1201:Reconfiguration. An out_of_frame, invalid_basis, repeated indeterminate or\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1210:### Refinement\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1286:### Complete enclosing-relation admission\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1292:validity, authority, currentness or transition can affect or be affected by\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1310:basis identity through admission. If validity or currentness can advance\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1312:and currentness law for that basis, or re-enters derivation and validation\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1333:an unidentified, stale or incoherently mixed basis; currentness can\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1338:### Standing structural qualification\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1348:| Form | Required observation |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1350:| direct | the complete direct relation is derived, validated and admitted once |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1359:| atomic publication failure | after validation succeeds, failure or interruption is observed at every materially distinct commit or publication boundary capable of exposing a subset, followed by fresh reconstruction showing the complete transition or none; named representative observations suffice only under a design-declared dominance or equivalence proof covering the complete partial-failure surface |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1366:observation or a declared coverage proof, a case uses a weaker helper or a\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1370:## 5. Work state and restart\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1422:incompleteness blocks a closed causal cone; if a same-process test is used\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1438:| P0 (recovered), P3 (independent), P4b (derived from P0 and P2, with P0's premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable), P6 (independent); instance premises a, c | By P0 an actor's context is bounded and disposable, by P3 the workspace binds the exact state, and by P4b recorded facts persist where the context does not, so the workspace is the truth surface and an actor's context a disposable account of it; current evidence corrects the account; discarding the account resets nothing | [The workspace and an actor's account](#the-workspace-and-an-actors-account) | the observations and reconciliations a resumption needs: the recovery contract, which is the resuming step's intake with the work state | 6, 9 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1441:| P4b (derived from P0 and P2, with P0's premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable), P0 (recovered), P6 (independent); instance premise c | By P4b and P0 private working context does not survive the actor, and by P6 a reused judgment is not a new independent one, so handoff is by closed results without private working context; reuse checks exact applicability and three invalidators, a material input change (newly acquired material evidence included), a changed basis and a declared revising observation, and a domain trigger is an instance of one of them; a reused judgment does not satisfy a required independent judgment | [§7](#7-closed-result-and-reuse) | the revising observation a result declares, and its other invalidation conditions: the producer of that result | 7, 9 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1448:- Row 1, work state as an object: [§1 Transitions](#transitions), where the current state is the work state this section records; [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Not performed, and [Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation), where unresolved work and an unexercised capability are a state of the work, carried as a residual and not a result; [WORLD_MODEL §14](WORLD_MODEL.md#14-results-of-this-profile), where a step's work state carries an unrun verification as a residual; [REFERENCE_FRAME §10 Revision actions](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#revision-actions), where results reopened without a material revision are recorded in the work state; [UX §8 Msg-replay proof](UX.md#msg-replay-proof), whose Msg log is the surface's recorded work state, and the [UX family table](UX.md#foundation-to-law), whose row for continuation and replay imports F4; the [ODD family table](ODD.md#foundation-to-law), whose rows for the immutable ledger and for yield import F4 for a replay-visible work state.\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1450:- Row 3, resumption and effects of uncertain completion: [§1 Construction relation](#construction-relation), Control, where resumption reacquires current reality and unknown effects are resolved before the next dependent action; [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §12 step 4](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#4-executive-evaluates-the-work-result), [§7 The executive configuration](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#the-executive-configuration), failure assumptions, and [§13 Handoff projection](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#13-handoff-projection), whose work result names each intended effect with its value, and the [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE family table](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#foundation-to-law), whose row for the effect field imports F4 for the reconciliation; [PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4 Explicit complete consumer update](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#explicit-complete-consumer-update), where an update of uncertain completion is reconciled from the presented preimages before any repetition; [SPEC_METHOD §4 Computed classification and treatment](SPEC_METHOD.md#computed-classification-and-treatment), where a retry waits on that reconciliation; [TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE Closed constraint, judgment, residual and stop kinds](TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#closed-constraint-judgment-residual-and-stop-kinds) and [Mutable-subject effect relation](TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#mutable-subject-effect-relation), where an effect whose end is not established is reconciled before any repetition; [FOUNDATIONS §4 Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse), where recovery reacquires current reality and need not erase valid work; [CONFORMANCE §4](CONFORMANCE.md#4-cases-for-method-discriminators), case CD-03, and [§5](CONFORMANCE.md#5-discriminator-coverage), discriminators 38 and 39.\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1458:### The workspace and an actor's account\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1464:projection of the state (§2); revisable, because an observati