{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/var/folders/rz/r6wxvr0n15d906k2s0jw8j2h0000gn/T/stdo-skills-recovery-980mjkdm/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 df795635470aa29b2a6542fc8d598a8797ee9138b24f73764c0c5f1f06f9ca38 --principal host call --request - <<'STDO_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"continuation-acquire-support-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[938,967]}}}}\nSTDO_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:23dd247f68b8cb9eaf436315e788c3838432dd52bd005147a5f26868be458457\",\"sha256\":\"23dd247f68b8cb9eaf436315e788c3838432dd52bd005147a5f26868be458457\"},\"id\":\"continuation-acquire-support-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=e0ab1d510316bb810b5166884a2c4822ec54e08d4f18790d688c5a6374ce59ec]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 3. Step results and disposition\\n\\nA step returns its results in the core algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results): each evaluation it\\nperformed returns one core value with its predicate and domain outcome,\\nand an evaluation it did not perform has no result. The outcomes of\\nadmitting and activating a step, and the step's own outcomes, answer other\\nquestions than its evaluations do. This section owns them as five\\nrefinements of the core. Each names the question it answers and the\\npredicate its mapping is for, and maps each of its values to exactly one\\ncore value; the predicate travels with the value, so no refinement's\\n`satisfied` counts toward another predicate\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results)).\\nPurpose and material relation: admission, work, decisions and effects\\nstand in the one core (P5, P6), so a consumer that combines them cannot\\nread a refused activation as a step's stop, availability as fitness or\\nacceptance, a carried ambiguity as resolved, or an unknown effect as none.\\n\\n| Refinement | Question | Predicate of the mapping |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| admission and activation | may the step begin | the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact subject and basis |\\n| construction availability | did the step yield its output | a candidate is available |\\n| disposition | what the decision owner does with an assessed candidate | the candidate is accepted at its declared boundary |\\n| ambiguity outcome | what happened to a declared ambiguity | the declared ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis |\\n| effects | did an intended external effect occur | the intended effect occurred |\\n\\nA profile that refines these values for its own units maps each of its\\nvalues to exactly one core value under FOUNDATIONS §4 Results and adds no\\ncore value.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[938,967]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"32edac7552c461d5b248d9a395a60e945bf265113beb816bd0005f6ac4adb26d\",\"size_bytes\":1834,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[938,967]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/var/folders/rz/r6wxvr0n15d906k2s0jw8j2h0000gn/T/stdo-skills-recovery-980mjkdm/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 df795635470aa29b2a6542fc8d598a8797ee9138b24f73764c0c5f1f06f9ca38 --principal host call --request - <<'STDO_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"continuation-acquire-support-2\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1002,1048]}}}}\nSTDO_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:79d0957de657682ec9945a4a45d3869768a48e153d6da84450fe8d9b16c832aa\",\"sha256\":\"79d0957de657682ec9945a4a45d3869768a48e153d6da84450fe8d9b16c832aa\"},\"id\":\"continuation-acquire-support-2\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=dafb1860675a5e6c4a3140df632c0b2b225d7dca5450c0ae918b6d54671b3025]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Construction availability\\n\\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\\n\\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\\n\\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\\n\\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\\n\\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never\\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\\n(P5, P6).\\n\\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\\nP3).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1002,1048]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"f1716d7080e823fa4d3b92070a88c2a2e61dfc9bc96a597b36707c3d5d759e48\",\"size_bytes\":2888,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1002,1048]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/var/folders/rz/r6wxvr0n15d906k2s0jw8j2h0000gn/T/stdo-skills-recovery-980mjkdm/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 df795635470aa29b2a6542fc8d598a8797ee9138b24f73764c0c5f1f06f9ca38 --principal host call --request - <<'STDO_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"continuation-acquire-support-3\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1370,1400]}}}}\nSTDO_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/var/folders/rz/r6wxvr0n15d906k2s0jw8j2h0000gn/T/stdo-skills-recovery-980mjkdm/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 df795635470aa29b2a6542fc8d598a8797ee9138b24f73764c0c5f1f06f9ca38 --principal host call --request - <<'STDO_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"continuation-acquire-support-3\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1370,1400]}}}}\nSTDO_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:f45492b4794db4f380026ed89fbbc6d6241fb1c2c538e1c1ce07aa647d696d32\",\"sha256\":\"f45492b4794db4f380026ed89fbbc6d6241fb1c2c538e1c1ce07aa647d696d32\"},\"id\":\"continuation-acquire-support-3\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=c3eec4441dffac8766fb7bffce6f03a2e3d2ac031d0d26d82641915f09ff5f38]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 5. Work state and restart\\n\\nWork state is the tuple of: the current persistent workspace; the governing\\nbasis; the applicable closed results and judgments with their invalidators;\\nthe residuals; and the known uncertainty over external effects. It is an\\nobject (P3); its carrier (files, an event stream, another admitted owner) is\\na profile or realisation choice. Resumption, checkpointing and the\\nprogress account of this section are generic procedures\\n([SPEC_METHOD §11](SPEC_METHOD.md#11-build-tenant-binding)): they require\\nno particular carrier (P1, P6).\\n\\nResumption is re-entry of the same method over the current work state,\\nstarting from the current material state, by a possibly different actor.\\nIt recovers applicable progress, re-checks the invalidators of each reused\\nresult (§7), reopens only affected support, and reconciles uncertain\\nexternal effects, sufficiently for the next dependent action, before any\\nrepetition or dependent action. Resumption does not imply idempotence: an\\naction whose external effect may have occurred is not repeated blindly;\\nthe lawful next moves are reconciliation, yield or stop.\\n\\nCheckpoint. Acceptance binds one exact checkpoint. The next\\nalready-authorised bounded action may begin without renewed human approval;\\nacceptance does not widen the selected outcome or the affected relation set\\n(P6, P2). A preservation checkpoint may retain unfinished or unaccepted\\nwork under an existing exact operation grant; it identifies its parent or\\npredecessor, the included territory, the concurrent-writer disposition and\\nthe durable evidence location, and it is neither acceptance, promotion nor\\npublication. A proposed restart, which reconstructs from less than the\\nretained work, identifies why repair of retained work is insufficient,\\nwhich obligations and evidence survive, and which causal assumptions\\nchange; reconstructability alone does not select reconstruction. The work state and reconciliation\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1370,1400]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"63309e48dad989ed12376050995d07879af30d58bfec59ab2958b705721eda8f\",\"size_bytes\":1947,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1370,1400]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
